   "title": "25.1 Module 25 Introduction: The Cold War Turns Hot",
   "description": "<div id=\"sparkled-assessment\"><div style=\"background:#0A1226; border-bottom:4px solid #FFB347; border-radius:10px; padding:18px 22px; margin-bottom:12px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px; color:#FFB347; margin-bottom:6px;\"><strong>MODULE INTRODUCTION</strong></div><div style=\"font-family:'Old Standard TT',Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif; font-size:26px; color:#FFFDF8; line-height:1.25; margin-bottom:6px;\">Module Introduction: The Cold War Turns Hot</div><div style=\"font-size:15px; color:#FFB347;\">Survey · 2 questions · not graded</div></div>\n<div style=\"text-align:center; color:#FFB347; font-size:16px; margin:0 0 4px;\">◎ ─ ◎ ─ ◎</div>\n<div style=\"border-top:2px solid #B5440A; margin:0 0 16px;\"></div>\n<div style=\"background:#FFFDF8; border:1px solid #E2D6C6; border-top:4px solid #0A1226; border-radius:12px; padding:18px 22px; margin-bottom:14px;\"><div style=\"display:inline-block; background:#0A1226; color:#FFFDF8; font-size:12px; padding:4px 10px; border-radius:999px; margin-bottom:12px;\"><strong>Before you start</strong></div><p style=\"font-size:17px; color:#1B1A1A; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 0;\">Welcome to The Cold War Turns Hot. Answer the questions below before you open the first lesson. Your answers help your teacher see where the class is starting. This survey is not graded.</p></div>\n<div style=\"background:#FFFDF8; border:1px solid #E2D6C6; border-left:5px solid #B5440A; border-radius:12px; padding:14px 18px; margin-bottom:14px;\"><div style=\"font-size:13px; color:#B5440A; margin-bottom:6px;\"><strong>This module's goals:</strong></div><ul style=\"font-size:17px; color:#1B1A1A; line-height:1.6; margin:0; padding-left:26px;\"><li style=\"margin-bottom:6px;\">Explain how the Communists won China and how the Korean and Vietnam wars began and grew.</li><li style=\"margin-bottom:6px;\">Describe how Cuba became a Soviet ally and what happened in the thirteen days of October 1962.</li><li style=\"margin-bottom:0;\">Weigh the part played by judgment, bargaining, and luck in avoiding nuclear war.</li></ul></div>\n</div>",
