 "discussions": [
  {
   "title": "25.8 Discussion: Who blinked in Cuba?",
   "html": "<div id=\"sparkled-assessment\"><div style=\"background:#0A1226; border-bottom:4px solid #FFB347; border-radius:10px; padding:18px 22px; margin-bottom:12px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px; color:#FFB347; margin-bottom:6px;\"><strong>DISCUSSION</strong></div><div style=\"font-family:'Old Standard TT',Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif; font-size:26px; color:#FFFDF8; line-height:1.25; margin-bottom:6px;\">Who blinked in Cuba?</div><div style=\"font-size:16px; color:#FBE6D6; margin-bottom:6px;\">Kennedy’s patience, Khrushchev’s retreat, a secret bargain, or luck?</div><div style=\"font-size:15px; color:#FFB347;\">Graded discussion · 10 points · one post and one reply</div></div>\n<div style=\"text-align:center; color:#FFB347; font-size:16px; margin:0 0 4px;\">◎ ─ ◎ ─ ◎</div>\n<div style=\"border-top:2px solid #B5440A; margin:0 0 16px;\"></div>\n<div style=\"background:#FFFDF8; border:1px solid #E2D6C6; border-left:5px solid #B5440A; border-radius:12px; padding:14px 18px; margin-bottom:14px;\"><div style=\"font-size:13px; color:#B5440A; margin-bottom:6px;\"><strong>HOW TO WORK</strong></div><div style=\"font-size:16px; color:#1B1A1A; line-height:1.55;\">Read the two lessons and the two primary sources first, and look over your notes in My Notebook. Then post your answer to the prompt below, and reply to one classmate.</div></div>\n<div style=\"background:#FFFDF8; border:1px solid #E2D6C6; border-top:4px solid #0A1226; border-radius:12px; padding:18px 22px; margin-bottom:14px;\"><div style=\"display:inline-block; background:#0A1226; color:#FFFDF8; font-size:12px; padding:4px 10px; border-radius:999px; margin-bottom:12px;\"><strong>DISCUSSION PROMPT</strong></div><p style=\"font-size:17px; color:#1B1A1A; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 12px;\">This week’s question: Who blinked in Cuba, and why did the world survive?</p><p style=\"font-size:17px; color:#1B1A1A; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 12px;\">Choose one answer: Kennedy’s patience, Khrushchev’s retreat, the secret bargain over the missiles in Turkey, or luck. Use your chart. Name two decisions, with their dates and who made them, that support your answer. Then name one different choice that could have been made, such as taking General LeMay’s advice, and say what might have followed.</p><p style=\"font-size:17px; color:#1B1A1A; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 12px;\">Write 150 to 250 words. State one claim you believe is true. Then explain why, using the specific evidence named above. Keep to what the lessons and the sources show. If you are guessing, say so.</p><p style=\"font-size:17px; color:#1B1A1A; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 0;\">Then add one sentence on self-government. Two men held the power to begin a nuclear war. What does it take for a leader to rule himself, and the pressure around him, in such an hour? Use one decision from the lessons.</p></div>\n<div style=\"background:#FFFDF8; border:1px solid #E2D6C6; border-top:4px solid #6B4A2A; border-radius:12px; padding:18px 22px; margin-bottom:14px;\"><div style=\"display:inline-block; background:#6B4A2A; color:#FFFDF8; font-size:12px; padding:4px 10px; border-radius:999px; margin-bottom:12px;\"><strong>RESPOND TO A CLASSMATE</strong></div><p style=\"font-size:17px; color:#1B1A1A; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 0;\">Reply to one classmate. Do you agree with their reasoning? If so, strengthen it with a fact or decision they did not use. If not, say politely where you think it falls short, and give your reason.</p></div>\n<div style=\"background:#FFFDF8; border:1px solid #E2D6C6; border-top:4px solid #B5440A; border-radius:12px; padding:18px 22px; margin-bottom:14px;\"><div style=\"display:inline-block; background:#B5440A; color:#FFFDF8; font-size:12px; padding:4px 10px; border-radius:999px; margin-bottom:12px;\"><strong>GRADING RUBRIC (10 pts)</strong></div><table style=\"width:100%; border-collapse:collapse;\"><thead><tr style=\"background:#0A1226;\"><th style=\"padding:9px 12px; font-size:13px; color:#FFFDF8; text-align:left; border:1px solid #E2D6C6;\"></th></tr><tr style=\"background: #0E1C42;\">\n            <th style=\"padding: 9px 12px; font-size: 12px; color: #fff; text-align: left; border: 1px solid #334;\">Criteria</th><th style=\"padding:9px 12px; font-size:13px; color:#FFFDF8; text-align:left; border:1px solid #E2D6C6;\">Substantive (full credit)</th><th style=\"padding:9px 12px; font-size:13px; color:#FFFDF8; text-align:left; border:1px solid #E2D6C6;\">Thin (partial credit)</th><th style=\"padding:9px 12px; font-size:13px; color:#FFFDF8; text-align:left; border:1px solid #E2D6C6;\">Missing (no credit)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr style=\"background:#FFFDF8;\"><td style=\"padding:10px 12px; font-size:14px; color:#0A1226; border:1px solid #E2D6C6; width:150px; vertical-align:top;\">Your claim and your reasons<br><span style=\"font-size:12px; color:#B5440A;\">6 pts</span></td><td style=\"padding:10px 12px; font-size:14px; color:#1B1A1A; border:1px solid #E2D6C6; vertical-align:top;\">Takes a clear side, uses the specific evidence the prompt asks for, and explains why it supports the claim.</td><td style=\"padding:10px 12px; font-size:14px; color:#1B1A1A; border:1px solid #E2D6C6; vertical-align:top;\">Takes a side but gives general reasons, or leaves out part of what the prompt asks for.</td><td style=\"padding:10px 12px; font-size:14px; color:#1B1A1A; border:1px solid #E2D6C6; vertical-align:top;\">No post, or no claim.</td></tr><tr style=\"background:#FBF3E8;\"><td style=\"padding:10px 12px; font-size:14px; color:#0A1226; border:1px solid #E2D6C6; width:150px; vertical-align:top;\">Your reply to a classmate<br><span style=\"font-size:12px; color:#B5440A;\">4 pts</span></td><td style=\"padding:10px 12px; font-size:14px; color:#1B1A1A; border:1px solid #E2D6C6; vertical-align:top;\">Answers one classmate's actual reasoning. Strengthens it or says where it falls short, politely and with a reason.</td><td style=\"padding:10px 12px; font-size:14px; color:#1B1A1A; border:1px solid #E2D6C6; vertical-align:top;\">Replies, but only to agree or disagree with no reason.</td><td style=\"padding:10px 12px; font-size:14px; color:#1B1A1A; border:1px solid #E2D6C6; vertical-align:top;\">No reply.</td></tr></tbody></table><div style=\"text-align:right; margin-top:6px; font-size:13px; color:#B5440A;\">10 pts total</div></div>\n</div>",
